# Superpowers docs lifecycle

**This rule is always on.** It overrides Superpowers brainstorming / writing-plans defaults that open a new dated file every time. User/repo instructions take precedence over those skills.

`docs/superpowers/` holds living specs, open plans, HTML diagrams, and as-built product notes (e.g. `src-layout.md`). Module READMEs under `src/` / `build/` and **`docs/README.md`** remain entry points. This repo does **not** use mogu’s `docs/app|infra|common` four-pillar trees. There is **no** `docs/build/` tree.

## Default: revise in place (hard)

1. **Read** `docs/superpowers/README.md` (Active table — **only 9 living rows**), then the matching living umbrella, before any design write.
2. **One topic → one living spec.** New requirements are a new `§` (or checkbox under the linked plan) on that umbrella. **Do not** create `YYYY-MM-DD-*-design.md` for “another slice” of an existing topic.
3. Put **`Status: active | accepted | landed | superseded`** on the first metadata line of every edited living spec. Refresh **Updated:** when merging.
4. When a plan / umbrella work is fully done: **same change** move finished plan (and only then the living spec, if the whole topic is done) to `docs/superpowers/archive/{specs,plans}/` and put as-built facts in `docs/superpowers/` (or the module README).
5. Keep `docs/superpowers/README.md` as the **short Active table only**. Do not rebuild a full inventory in `docs/README.md`.

## Gate: when a **new** dated spec is allowed (rare)

Open a **new** `docs/superpowers/specs/YYYY-MM-DD-*-design.md` **only if all** hold:

1. It is a **new top-level subsystem** with **no** row in the Active table that can own it, **or** an **incompatible fork** that cannot be a `§` without lying.
2. The new file’s metadata names **which living file was considered** and **why a § merge is impossible** (one short paragraph). If that paragraph cannot be written honestly → **revise the living file**.
3. The topic is **not** covered by the ban list below.

If unsure → **revise the living umbrella**. Prefer wrong-umbrella `§` + later move over a new dated file.

### Ban list — never a new hot spec (use living `§` or as-built)

| Topic shape | Living umbrella |
| --- | --- |
| Subdirectory / scheme C layout / include break / dual-run file moves | Module `README.md` + `docs/superpowers/src-layout.md`, or a `§` under the owning living row |
| SP1–SP5 / SP1b / SP4b / leftover strangler / ABI cutover / DLL stems / GDI+ carto / two-finger pan | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-19-legacy-deep-abstraction-umbrella-design.md` |
| RHI / frame graph / GPU compose / P0 lit / map2d frame / atmosphere-weather / Skia canvas / render math / model-render-compute | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-13-render-rhi-scene-design.md` |
| `app/views` shell / capability dirs / Views toolkit / MFC migration / markup / compositor / GIS panels / debug console / WinUI·CEF rejects | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-27-views-desktop-shell-design.md` |
| `src/tool` module dirs / tool dispatch / tool behavior migration | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-13-tool-event-dispatch-design.md` |
| `src/base` / memory / PA-E / execution / archive / ipc-mojom / third-party JSON·XML·protobuf | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-14-base-root-hybrid-design.md` |
| GDAL / OGR DB / tile / SDB composition·style·subdir / sdbd / DataSession·Provider / china PLPT samples | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-13-gdal-layer-management-design.md` |
| Plugin host / full upgrade / subdir / product package | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-13-plugin-host-design.md` |
| Algorithm OSS layer | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-13-algorithm-layer-oss-design.md` |
| Net asio / httplib | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-13-net-asio-httplib-design.md` |

### Plans

- Prefer **plans linked from the living Active row** (checklists). Do not open a plan that only restates a layout move or duplicates an existing checklist.
- Brainstorming / writing-plans skills that default to a new dated file: **stop** and revise the living Active row (or append a `§` / checkbox) unless the Gate above passes.
- Milestone plans (`m0`–`m4`) are product checklists, **not** permission to open parallel design twins.

## Don’t

- **Don’t** add Topic 分册 / as-built stub files that only point at a longer design.
- **Don’t** open a parallel dated empty shell when a living umbrella already covers the shape.
- **Don’t** treat living `specs/` / `plans/` as the only as-built; keep product facts in the superpowers-root markdown files or module READMEs.
- **Don’t** rewrite archived bodies except mechanical link fixes.
- **Don’t** archive a living umbrella when unsure — leave it hot and add a `§`.
- **Don’t** reopen archived `superseded` / `landed` specs as living twins.
- **Don’t** ask the user to re-approve “which umbrella” when the ban list already maps the topic — pick the row and iterate.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `docs/superpowers/README.md` | Active living table (short; 9 rows) + as-built index |
| `docs/superpowers/*.md` (root) | As-built product notes (`src-layout`, UI testing, ABI map, …) |
| `docs/superpowers/specs/` | Living umbrellas only (`active` / `accepted`) |
| `docs/superpowers/plans/` | Open checklists hung off living rows |
| `docs/superpowers/diagrams/` | HTML layering / principle diagrams (living + as-built) |
| `docs/superpowers/archive/` | `landed` / `superseded` / fold-B children |

## Diagrams (always)

When a living `§` or plan **locks architecture / parallel model / layer ownership**, ship a companion HTML under `docs/superpowers/diagrams/` in the **same change** (core layering + principle flow; optional animation). See **`.cursor/rules/repo/design-html-diagrams.mdc`**.

